  "_comment": [
    "MovieHub sample catalogue. Titles, synopses and cast are INVENTED for this build —",
    "nothing here represents a licensed title (PRD §11.1). Shaped exactly like the",
    "`GET /home` + `GET /titles/{id}` responses so pointing BuildConfig.API_BASE_URL at a",
    "real host needs no model or mapper changes.",
    "",
    "Episode lists are generated by EpisodeFactory using the design's own formula",
    "(Catalog.jsx episodesOf): name = EP_NAMES[i % 26], dur = (38 + ((i * 7) % 9)) * 60 + 10.",
    "Enumerating ~200 episodes here would just duplicate that.",
    "",
    "Streams are free, public, multi-bitrate test assets — the §6.7 quality ladder is only",
    "real if there are renditions for setMaxVideoSize to choose between:",
    "  bipbop_16x9  416x234 / 640x360 / 960x540 / 1280x720 / 1920x1080 + en/es/fr/ja subtitles",
    "  mux_x36xhzz  320x184 / 512x288 / 848x480 / 1280x720 / 1920x1080",
    "  angel_one    192x144 / 320x240 / 480x360 / 640x480 / 768x576 + en subtitles (covers 144p/240p)",
    "  tears_dash   142 / 380 / 570 / 856 (DASH)",
    "",
    "All shipped content is clear. The per-title `drm` block below is fully supported",
    "end-to-end (playback, Widevine OFFLINE licence acquisition, real licence expiry);",
    "`drmTestVector` is the verified Axinom public test asset used to exercise that path",
    "from the debug build, so no shipped title can break if their token rotates."
